WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.240
I see. So you were in Seiran till now.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:16.750
Yeah. I heard that troops from
Togetsu were heading to Suoh.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.420
Fortunately, it wasn't
too late to stop them.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.000
You did that all on your own?

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Of course not.
I had Seiran's forces back me up.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.300
But enough about me.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.090
What's the situation on your end?

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:37.350
So the Kunad Gate is growing.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:40.770
And you exposed the Togetsu faith's
true nature and plans.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:46.320
And Kagero. What a shock to learn
you came from the moon 2,000 years ago.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:48.650
I look young for my age, don't I?

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:52.410
Nice work ferreting out all that info.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:55.780
You all exceeded my expectations,
including how you exploited Arahabaki.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:56.790
Thank you.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.580
What about Naomi?

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:00.160
And Nagi.

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.580
We have to stop Togetsu.

00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:05.880
Right.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:09.800
I still don't get
what Karen's trying to do.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:14.300
He used the Red Strings to travel
through time. That much is sure.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:19.770
Fubuki, Alice was at Seiran's Supernatural
Life Research Facility, wasn't she?

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:25.310
That's right. It was originally built
to return her to human form.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.650
So that Other really was Alice.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.030
What?

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.200
Are you saying...?

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:34.490
That's right.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:39.950
Alice was among the human-derived
Others that saved us.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:43.620
Aunt Alice was there? But...

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:49.090
Karen was most likely there to save Alice.

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:53.720
So I've failed once again.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:57.050
I'll hit reset as many times as it takes.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:02.270
So he traveled back in time to try and
stop Alice from turning into an Other?

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:05.150
But then why did he attack Yuito?

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:10.320
I bet he also needed Yuito's power
in order to use the Red Strings.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.900
He said, "As many times as it takes."

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:17.450
Does that mean he's traveled back
in time over and over again?

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.830
Karen, would you really go that far?

00:02:21.830 --> 00:02:28.250
Um, Aunt Alice was your fiancée,
wasn't she?

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.130
Yes.

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:32.800
Luka, is it okay if I tell them?

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:33.840
Yes.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:39.390
After all, we shouldn't keep secrets
from those we're working with.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:45.940
Alice was both a fellow OSF soldier

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:51.110
and a childhood friend of Karen and mine.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:55.450
We spent an awful lot of time together.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:58.620
The three of us were inseparable.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:34.250
Karen's Wish

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:35.840
Alice and I were still kids
when we first met Karen.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:38.670
Alice, are you really gonna go?

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:39.880
Yeah.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:44.100
I don't see what the big rush is.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.600
Our classmate, Maria,
has already been scouted.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.060
It's so frustrating.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:55.360
Just because she was scouted early
doesn't mean she'll make it into the OSF.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:00.450
I wanna be scouted early so I can join
the OSF and protect everyone!

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:05.240
I'm gonna go get tested now
and prove I have what it takes.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.790
You think they'll really test you?

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:14.710
That's why I asked my father--

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:24.090
Are you all right? Do you need a doctor?

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.470
Leave me alone!

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:39.110
I don't need anyone's help.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.780
What's his problem?

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:59.170
I knew they wouldn't test you.

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:09.260
You again? What do you want?

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:23.030
Let's go, Luka.

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:24.400
Okay.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:31.540
The next day, we still couldn't
stop thinking about him,

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:34.250
so we stopped by the hospital.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:44.420
He told us how he and his brother
had been hospitalized for some time.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:49.930
Though he seemed unfriendly at first,
we soon realized he was kind-hearted.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.060
I'm Alice Ichijo.

00:06:52.060 --> 00:06:54.140
I'm Fubuki Spring.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:56.770
What's your name?

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:00.190
Karen. Karen Travers.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:06.490
After that, Alice and I started
visiting the hospital every day.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:09.070
We soon grew close to Karen.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:11.330
And to you, too, Luka.

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:16.710
Why were you in the hospital?
And why the two of you together?

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:20.920
My brother and I were born
without any power.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:23.300
We were duds.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:25.050
You were duds?

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:31.430
It seems the subject also has
no memory of being a dud.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:33.600
Did you know?

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:36.600
Yeah, Karen told us.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.810
I see.

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:40.730
My brother and I

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:44.780
were subjected to experiments
that could give us psionic powers.

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:51.160
They treated us like lab rats.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:58.580
The only thing that gave us hope
in our darkest hours

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:01.250
was Alice and Fubuki's friendship.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:04.130
They told us about the world outside.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:08.550
We learned about school,
family, and friends.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:14.220
We knew nothing but life in the hospital,
so it all seemed impossibly beautiful.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:20.520
Perhaps we might join that world
if we could use psionic powers.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:24.770
That idea was what kept us going.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:28.780
You gave Alice and I courage, too.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:33.450
Karen's strength to carry on
despite great suffering inspired us.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:35.990
What's wrong?

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:39.750
Another one of her classmates
was scouted by the OSF.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:44.000
Is my power really that weak?

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:58.270
Alice's psionic power is Genesis.

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:00.060
What's yours?

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.650
Wow! That's amazing!

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:12.320
I want to join the OSF
and work hard to help people.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.990
Nobody wants that more than me.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:19.910
Wimps like you will never see
their dreams come true.

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.000
I'm never gonna give up.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:26.540
I'm gonna do whatever it takes
to get out of here!

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.210
You're right.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:31.880
I gotta be strong like you!

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.550
Just don't overdo it.

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:36.680
Try everything you can to get discharged!

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:38.270
I can't wait!

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:41.890
I'm trying my hardest!

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:44.350
I can't wait, either.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:48.480
Then we can all be together forever.

00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:53.150
Fiancée? What's that?

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:56.200
It means we'll get married
when we grow up.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.830
Alice and Fubuki?

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:02.040
That's right. Our families
have already arranged it.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:10.170
They're so lucky.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.360
Karen!

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:33.740
That was a borderline response.
Continue the attack.

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.160
Roger that.

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:46.880
Karen?

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:48.290
I can't wait.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.880
We can all be together forever.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:17.030
What the hell?

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:43.350
What's that?

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:45.060
Karen.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:49.650
Did he just steal his power?

00:11:57.400 --> 00:12:01.740
Karen was scouted by
the OSF right after that.

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:08.960
I was scouted around the same time,
and we became comrades.

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:12.500
Karen!

00:12:25.270 --> 00:12:29.560
Alice later joined us in the OSF.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.980
Ta-da!

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:38.610
Alice Ichijo, official member
of the OSF, starting today!

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:41.070
Congratulations, Alice.

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.910
I finally caught up.

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.870
I'm gonna work hard to
keep up with you guys.

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:50.750
Just don't be one of those new recruits
who screws up after trying too hard.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:53.290
Oh, you mean like a certain soldier

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:57.800
who was recently reprimanded
for disobeying a superior officer?

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.840
Fubuki.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:02.510
It was your 50th reprimand.
Quite a milestone.

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:06.100
How could I keep such
a juicy tidbit to myself?

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:09.640
They say you're a shoo-in for Septentrion,

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:12.270
yet you don't see eye to eye
with your superiors.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:15.650
I've no intention of obeying
orders I disagree with.

00:13:15.650 --> 00:13:19.740
Then you should become
the head of the OSF.

00:13:19.740 --> 00:13:22.610
And babysit a bunch of weaklings?

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:25.120
I'll let Fubuki handle that.

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:29.120
So you say, but you actually do
look after your comrades.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:33.170
Then how about you two share the top spot?

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:34.710
Not a bad idea.

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:37.960
Karen can lead, and I'll serve
as his top lieutenant.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:41.260
Or we could switch to
a regiment structure and--

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:43.340
That's not for you to decide.

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:02.900
We fought in the same platoon,

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:05.910
and Alice grew ever more
formidable, just as we did.

00:14:27.890 --> 00:14:29.220
Are you okay?

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:30.430
Yeah.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:39.400
Um, thank you for saving me.

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:41.070
Stay focused.

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:42.940
Right. Sorry.

00:14:42.940 --> 00:14:46.700
How many times have you come to my rescue?

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:49.080
Are you two okay?

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:50.580
Fubuki!

00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:53.040
Glad to see you're all right.

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:57.580
She screwed up again, like an idiot.

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.710
Bit off more than you could chew again?

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:04.010
You should be more careful
for your own sake.

00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:05.680
Karen, you're hurt?!

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:08.050
This is all my fault. Let's have a look.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:10.220
No need. It's barely a scratch.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:15.390
Fubuki, Alice is tired.
Go make sure she gets some rest.

00:15:15.390 --> 00:15:18.100
I'll go check on the other teams.

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:19.770
Wait, Karen!

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:25.610
Then a rare phenomenon
occurred two years later.

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:33.120
In certain areas, the Extinction Belt
descended to an extremely low elevation.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:37.000
Brain talk doesn't work right now,
so let's be careful.

00:15:58.310 --> 00:15:59.310
I'm going ahead!

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:01.900
Karen, don't go too far!

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:06.740
I've got this. Alice, you back Karen up.

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:07.950
Roger that!

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:41.190
Karen!

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:52.740
Alice!

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:54.990
Alice? Alice!

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:05.710
Alice!

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:12.890
Alice?

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:26.020
What the--?

00:17:26.020 --> 00:17:28.360
Alice...

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:34.030
Alice! Is that you?!

00:17:34.030 --> 00:17:35.660
Stop! Alice!

00:18:07.360 --> 00:18:10.240
Just like my sister.

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:14.570
After that, Alice was confined
to the OSF Hospital.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:18.240
They treated her like
some sort of guinea pig.

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:23.620
Only the government and a few
in the OSF knew about it.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:29.130
Break Alice out of the hospital?!

00:18:30.210 --> 00:18:33.630
Do you realize what will
happen if you do that?

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:40.770
Don't try and stop me.
I'll go it alone if you won't help.

00:18:40.770 --> 00:18:45.560
What will you do with her after that?

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:50.030
My family's firm, Spring Pharmaceuticals,
has connections in Seiran.

00:18:50.030 --> 00:18:52.070
They might be able to help.

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:59.700
With Seiran's help,
we were able to rescue Alice.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:05.580
But she faced a lengthy lockup after that.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:13.420
In trying to save her, did we end up
forcing an even worse fate upon her?

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:15.840
That thought haunted me.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:22.560
I begged Karen to put an end to this.

00:19:22.560 --> 00:19:25.980
But he wouldn't listen.

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:29.400
He said he'd save Alice at all costs.

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:33.490
Then we can all be together forever.

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:40.240
Karen is trying to change
Alice's fate by altering the past.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.240
You're probably right.

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:45.370
Karen definitely did travel through time.

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:48.120
But Alice still ended up dead.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:52.880
He traveled to the past,
but he couldn't change history?

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:55.550
His plan didn't work?

00:19:55.550 --> 00:20:00.470
I don't know, but we have
to do what we can now.

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:01.850
I agree.

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:05.140
Right. Karen is definitely a concern.

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:08.270
But stopping Togetsu is
the more pressing matter.

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:09.900
But how?

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:15.280
What if we try to shut down
Togetsu's control computer, BABE?

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:19.360
Their Red Strings research
and plan implementation data

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:21.870
is all on BABE.

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:27.000
You guys currently have
the clearest grasp of the situation.

00:20:27.000 --> 00:20:29.330
I'll leave it up to you.

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:33.750
While you deal with Togetsu,
is there anything I can do?

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:37.260
Can you act as an intermediary
between Suoh and Seiran?

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:42.600
Even just easing the conflict between
them should limit Togetsu's options.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:45.890
So you want me to convince
them to sign a ceasefire?

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:49.850
Suoh and Seiran don't trust Togetsu.

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:53.730
Use that mistrust,
and you just might succeed.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:54.900
It's worth a shot.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:57.820
Just don't get in over your head.

00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:00.490
Same with you, Sis.

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:02.910
So we have to infiltrate Togetsu.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:04.740
What's the plan?

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:10.500
Let's use what Kagero and Kyoka know about
the place to come up with something.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:13.250
I'm counting on you two.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:15.500
Okay, leave it to us.

00:21:17.340 --> 00:21:18.670
Kagero?

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:20.720
Huh? Oh, yeah, I'm in.

00:21:28.020 --> 00:21:30.520
That cavern should prove useful again.

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:33.480
The one we used to escape?

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:37.150
You're not planning on battling
that Other again, are you?

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:39.070
What do you think, Kagero?

00:21:39.070 --> 00:21:46.580
Sorry, but can we postpone
this strategy meeting till later?

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:51.000
Yuito, I need to talk to you
before we go to Togetsu.

00:21:51.000 --> 00:21:52.370
Me?

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:56.170
Not here. Let's step outside.

00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:59.880
You guys might as well hear this, too.

00:22:03.260 --> 00:22:05.300
What did you want to say?

00:22:06.850 --> 00:22:12.140
It's about your father,
Chairman Joe Sumeragi.

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:14.730
My dad?

00:22:14.730 --> 00:22:17.690
I know who killed him.

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:18.980
It was me.

00:22:18.980 --> 00:22:20.190
Huh?

00:22:33.960 --> 00:22:41.800
<i>I've been a prisoner</i>
<i>of my own longing</i>

00:22:43.590 --> 00:22:51.390
<i>The shimmering heat signals me to halt</i>

00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:53.520
<i>There's a stranger in me</i>

00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:56.020
<i>I'll fly high so I won't be scared</i>

00:22:56.020 --> 00:23:01.280
<i>By this new self I've never seen</i>

00:23:01.280 --> 00:23:03.070
<i>I'm spreading my wings</i>

00:23:03.070 --> 00:23:05.410
<i>Bird in florid flight</i>

00:23:05.410 --> 00:23:10.120
<i>Lift your eyes to the scarlet sky</i>

00:23:10.120 --> 00:23:15.330
<i>Overtaken by the mighty wind</i>

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:20.500
<i>The view unfolds upon a world</i>
<i>that begins turning</i>

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:24.970
<i>Amid the intermingling light</i>

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:30.850
<i>I keep searching for tomorrow</i>

00:23:30.850 --> 00:23:32.470
<i>Tomorrow's in your hands</i>

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:35.690
<i>Don't tell me now you're afraid</i>

00:23:35.690 --> 00:23:37.310
<i>There's no time to waste</i>

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:40.270
<i>Keep going forward</i>

00:23:40.270 --> 00:23:44.610
<i>There's nothing to be afraid of</i>

00:23:44.610 --> 00:23:46.280
<i>Now, let's go</i>

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:51.740
<i>Into a brand-new day</i>

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:11.970
Kagero's Confession
